  "summary": [
    "Set-valued simple cuts: edges of E(G) meeting both S and its complement. Packing X47 uses the same intersection body over the M1 edge alias; Cycle X212 uses the equivalent count-one formula, proved equal on two-element simple edges. X47 cut connectivity is the unguarded forall-nonempty-proper-side lower bound, true for every k at orders 0 and 1; it is not deletion connectivity without its 1 < #|G| guard. Existing common.cut_size is reused through the exact cardinality bridge.",
